  "articleBody": "It's easy to make missteps when you're under stress after a drug crime arrest, but some common mistakes can seriously hurt your case. First, don't talk to law enforcement without your attorney present. Anything you say can and will be used against you, even if you think you're just being cooperative. Second, resist the urge to destroy or hide any evidence; this can lead to additional charges. Third, don't ignore court dates or legal notices; missing them can result in warrants or harsher penalties. Fourth, avoid discussing your case on social media or with friends and family, as these conversations aren't privileged and could be subpoenaed. Fifth, don't assume your case is hopeless; there are often many avenues for defense. Finally, don't delay in seeking legal counsel. An experienced drug crime defense attorney can advise you on your rights, guide you through the process, and build a strong defense. The sooner you get professional help, the better your chances are for a positive resolution.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-26"
